# The influence of N.G.’s ideas Alexandrova on the civil theory of legal relations

**Authors:** S.V. Tretyakov

## Abstract
N.G. Alexandrov is a prominent Russian legal scholar who has greatly contributed to the development of the spear field of private law theory – the doctrine of legal relationship. His chief contributions have been summarised und their ramifications have been examined in this piece. There three basic areas where the impact of N.G. Alexandrov’s ideas seems to be the most profound and enduring. Primarily, the concept of legal relationship viewed as an epiphenomenon of legal rules, special mode of realisation of law, strongly influenced by the German imperative theory of the 19th century. Secondly, a narrow definition of subjective right as identical to the Hohfeldian claim-right. Thirdly, a strong emphasis on the correlativity of rights and duties, both logical and existential. A special reference has been made to the issue of private law.

